      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Project links\n\n- [WCCKIT GitHub repository](https://github.com/razman786/wcckit)\n- [AMD μProf](https://www.amd.com/en/developer/uprof.html)\n- [Intel PCM](https://github.com/intel/pcm)\n- [BCC/eBPF tools](https://github.com/iovisor/bcc)\n"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "noValue": "Disabled: No data"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Run A Collector",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 11
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Collector quick commands\n\nOn the compute node, open the SSH tunnel from the laptop first, then attach to a pipeline PID.\n\nIntel CPU:\n```bash\ndockerfiles/bin/run-wcckit-intel-overview.sh \\\n  --pid \"$PID\" --pipeline DDFacet --language python \\\n  --max-duration 60 --influx-url http://127.0.0.1:18086\n```\n\nAMD CPU:\n```bash\ndockerfiles/bin/run-wcckit-amd-overview.sh \\\n  --pid \"$PID\" --pipeline DDFacet --language python \\\n  --max-duration 60 --influx-url http://127.0.0.1:18086 \\\n  --amd-uprof-power\n```\n\nUse `--match DDFacet` instead of `--pid \"$PID\"` when WCCKIT should choose the newest matching process.\n"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "noValue": "Disabled: No data"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
